<recipe>
<title>Paneer chickpea curry</title>
<serves>Serves six.</serves>
<prep>Preheat a slow cooker.</prep>

<ingredients>
<i><q>1</q><n>onion</n></i>
<i><q>2 cloves</q><n>garlic</n></i>
<i><q>1 x 400 g tin</q><n>diced tomatoes</n></i>
<i><q>1 x 440 mL tin</q><n>coconut milk</n></i>
<i><q>1 C</q><n>stock (vegetable or chicken)</n></i>
<i><q>large pinch</q><n>salt</n></i>
<i><q>large grind</q><n>pepper</n></i>
<i><q>1/2 tsp</q><n>turmeric</n></i>
<i><q>1 tsp</q><n>chili powder</n></i>
<i><q>1 tsp</q><n>ground coriander</n></i>
<i><q>2 tsp</q><n>garam masala</n></i>
<i><q>1.5</q><n>red capsicum, roughly chopped</n></i>
<i><q>1/3</q><n>butternut squash, diced or grated</n></i>
<i><q>3</q><n>carrots, peeled and diced</n></i>
<i><q>3 or 4</q><n>parsnips, peeled and diced</n></i>
<i><q>1 x 400 g tin</q><n>chickpeas</n></i>
<i><q>200 g</q><n>paneer, diced</n></i>
<i><q>large handful</q><n>baby spinach, roughly chopped</n></i>
</ingredients>

<method>
<s>Dice onion and gently fry with garlic to soften.  Add spices and cook until fragrant.</s>
<s>Add chopped tomatoes, coconut milk, stock, salt and pepper.  Combine well.</s>
<s>Blend with a stick blender.</s>
<s>Add vegetables, chickpeas and paneer.  Bring to a boil, then transfer to slow cooker.</s>
<s>Cook for three hours on high.</s>
<s>Stir through chopped spinach shortly before serving.</s>
<s>Serve with steamed rice and fresh coriander.</s>
</method>

</recipe>